# Sync backend docs with the client repo

Whenever this API changes (feature, bug fix, route, policy, health, Swagger, or live URL), update **`README.md` and screenshots in this repo and the matching files in the client repo** in the same effort. Keep both sides aligned.

## Same change must cover

- `README.md` — short project description at the top, live URLs, tech stack, routes, models, policies
- `docs/screenshots/live/` — status page, `/api/v1/health`, `/api/docs`
- `docs/screenshots/auth|admin|user/` — portal screens (keep in sync with the frontend capture)
- Client sibling: `../client/README.md` (shared blurb + URLs) and `../client/docs/screenshots/`

If UI or live endpoints changed, recapture from the client repo:

```bash
cd ../client && node scripts/capture-screens.mjs
```

That script copies the full screenshot tree into `docs/screenshots/` here.

## Do not

- Do not invent features that are not in the code
- Do not commit secrets (Mongo/Redis/JWT) into README
- Do not update only this README when shared product text, URLs, or screens changed
- Do not uncomment Cursor-rule notes in README (keep them HTML-commented)
